Subject: [Krypton] Preserve Chromium menu component data across the UI ABI

Capture the complete MenuModel presentation data, including hidden rows,
secondary/accessibility labels, minor icons, color roles, font fallback and
render parameters, accelerators, badges, groups and button rows. Keep source
ids separate from invocation tokens and invalidate captured commands when
their model changes. Capture does not take ownership of browser menu models.

The replacement presenter needs the same minor-icon placement query as the
original Views presenter. Grant that narrow passkey access without changing
MenuModel behavior, exposing the passkey publicly or inventing a default.

--- a/ui/base/models/menu_model.h
+++ b/ui/base/models/menu_model.h
@@ -33,6 +33,10 @@
 }  // namespace examples
 
 }  // namespace views
+namespace krypton_ui {
+class MenuModelSnapshot;
+}
+
 namespace ui {
 
 class Accelerator;
@@ -79,6 +83,7 @@
     // These cases are exclusively the ones allowed to use the feature.
     friend class ::OmniboxContextMenuController;
     friend class ::views::MenuModelAdapter;
+    friend class ::krypton_ui::MenuModelSnapshot;
     friend class ::ui::SimpleMenuModel;
     // This item is here merely for testing and example of this feature.
     friend class ::views::examples::ExampleMenuModel;
